## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical use of IAM DB authentication, RDS Proxy, and fine-grained access controls across accounts, plus a concrete testing plan.

## Key Concepts
- IAM database authentication with Aurora PostgreSQL
- RDS Proxy for serverless/large-concurrency access
- Fine-grained grants and per-service DB users
- Cross-account role mappings and network isolation
- Validation: latency, authorization, and failover tests

## Code Example
```sql
CREATE USER sales_read LOGIN;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA sales TO sales_read;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA sales TO sales_read;

CREATE USER orders_rw LOGIN;
GRANT INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA orders TO orders_rw;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA orders TO orders_rw;
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA orders GRANT INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON TABLES TO orders_rw;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify IAM role to DB user mapping using Lambda? 
- What monitoring would you set to detect privilege drift or misconfiguration?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to perform online schema migrations in Aurora PostgreSQL Global Database, considering cross-region replication, lag, and non-blocking operations. It probes knowledge of: adding nullable columns, backfilling, CONCURRENTLY indexing, failover testing, latency impact, and DR readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Online DDL in Aurora PostgreSQL
- Concurrent index creation
- Backfill in batches
- Cross-region replication lag
- DR validation and failover testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Add nullable column (non-blocking)
ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN audit JSONB NULL;

// Backfill in batches (simulate in app or script)
UPDATE orders SET audit = '{}' WHERE audit IS NULL;

// Create a concurrently built index
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_orders_audit ON orders USING GIN (audit);

// After backfill, enforce NOT NULL and default for future writes
ALTER TABLE orders ALTER COLUMN audit SET NOT NULL;
ALTER TABLE orders ALTER COLUMN audit SET DEFAULT '{}';
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt if there is a dependent materialized view?
- What are edge cases with NOT NULL in multi-region clusters and how would you mitigate them?
